  "revised": "2026-11-13",
  "source": "Extension xS11 Modbus map v2.0, Unipi technology",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Extension xS11 Modbus map",
      "version": "2.0",
      "url": "https://kb.unipi.technology/_media/files:products:extensions:unipi-extension-xs11-modbus-map-v2.0.pdf",
      "note": "Holding registers, Coils and Description sheets"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Registers are 0-based. 32-bit values use word order CDAB (low word first). Defaults: slave address 15, 19200 bps, 8N1.",
    "Registers marked Reserved in the manual are left out.",
    "Tested on an Extension xS11 (firmware register 0x0608), November 2026, over Modbus RTU. All registers that can be read answered; the coils that only trigger an action were not read. The input and output counts (12 and 13), the debounce scale (raw 50 reads 5 ms) and the low-word-first order of the serial number agree with the manual. The counters were 0, so their word order was not checked. The module did not support FC17, and it answered on a different address and baud rate than its address and baud rate registers show, so those two registers were not confirmed against the live settings."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 15,
  "baudrate": 19200,
  "parity": "N",
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
  "address_base": 0,
